## TDD evidence

Isolated branch `ci/track6-system-optimization-activity-verify`. RED `916e90731a7437e04bdaf0bc6aa85a1098e22b93`, run `36630504421`, job `109618218721`: native PASS; managed build failed with eight expected missing-symbol errors for the new activity API, zero compiler warnings. A contract-only intermediate commit/run was incomplete by construction. Final GREEN `a6600eec7c25f9b16e188ca3405f02a41d6f42cb`, run `36630781473`, job `109619394152`: all native, managed, Core, App, publish and upload steps SUCCESS.

Official selective commit `78ee8384957f174824228d958be0d52c392d3ae2` contains exactly four code/test files: new `SystemOptimizationActivityProbe.cs`, instrumented `SystemOptimizationTransactionEngine.cs`, new cross-instance self-test, and one Program registration. Temporary verifier workflow excluded.

## Proven behavior

`SystemOptimizationActivitySnapshot` carries a process-wide generation and active-operation count. State is Active while count > 0. `ProvesUninterruptedIdle` requires both snapshots idle and identical generation. All `SystemOptimizationTransactionEngine` instances share one static observer state. `BeginSessionAsync`, `ApplyPersistentAsync` and `RestoreAsync` enter observation only after their per-instance transaction gate is acquired; exit always advances generation and decrements active count.

The tests prove a second engine instance's operation is visible while active and remains detectable after it completes between two idle snapshots. Existing per-engine transaction serialization, dependency ownership, snapshots, rollback and History behavior are unchanged.

## Limits and continuation

This is detection of DG System Optimization operations inside this process, not mutual exclusion and not external Windows mutation evidence. Regedit, vendor tools, driver panels, other applications and kernel/driver changes are not covered. It is not yet consumed by the generic canary.

Next TDD integrates this observer into `GenericGuardianWindowsSessionCanaryExecutor`: pre-mutation intervals require unchanged idle generation; successful own `BeginSessionAsync` must account for exactly one operation entry+exit (+2 generation, idle after); any additional overlapping/completed DG operation causes deny before mutation or rollback Inconclusive/no KEEP after mutation. A later owner host must provide actual exclusion and retained-lease cleanup. FF/BlueStacks scene evidence remains unsupported, so generic activation remains disabled.

This documentary commit requires fresh exact-head Windows CI before being marked verified.
